12:56.380 --> 13:01.400
It sucks in about six different
feeds and updates your iTunes.

13:01.400 --> 13:04.000
And if you have it, an iPod
automatically.

13:04.000 --> 13:13.440
I'm going to be working on the
next release where there will be
a separate text file sitting in
the iPodder folder.

13:13.440 --> 13:15.160
And that's going to be your
subscription file.

13:15.300 --> 13:22.660
So all you do is basically just
add a new line with a URL to it
to any MP3 enclosure feed with
MP3 files.

13:22.660 --> 13:27.320
And it'll automatically run
through that file as well.

13:27.320 --> 13:31.320
It'll parse it and download the
enclosures when you run the
iPodder application.

13:31.320 --> 13:35.840
After that, so that'll probably
be about release beta 06,

13:35.840 --> 13:45.180
I hope to just have some form of
installer that sets it all up
for you and runs the program at
a set interval.

13:45.180 --> 13:47.100
with one configuration file

13:48.000 --> 13:49.560
And you never hear from it
again.

13:49.560 --> 13:52.640
It just keeps running
automatically at the intervals
that you set.

13:52.640 --> 13:56.740
And I think I mentioned in the
previous show

13:56.740 --> 13:58.420
that it looks like some
developers out there

13:58.420 --> 14:00.840
are working on their own
versions.

14:00.840 --> 14:02.940
Some Python stuff.

14:02.940 --> 14:04.260
I'm looking forward to that
coming out.

14:04.260 --> 14:06.100
Please, make this better than I
did.

14:06.100 --> 14:08.680
Let's see.

14:08.680 --> 14:10.000
That's about it.

14:10.000 --> 14:10.340
Let me see.

14:10.340 --> 14:11.380
I've been at this for...

14:11.380 --> 14:11.940
How long are we going to talk?

14:11.940 --> 14:12.580
14 minutes?

14:12.580 --> 14:13.680
Okay, no song of the day.

14:13.680 --> 14:17.640
Besides, enough copyright
violation with that bit from the
timeline audiobook.

14:17.640 --> 14:22.880
But I'm going to go fill up the
server with some more content.

14:22.880 --> 14:26.320
See if I can now connect the
bridge on that

14:26.320 --> 14:30.100
so that if a new video comes in
as a torrent,

14:30.100 --> 14:31.080
bit torrent file,

14:31.080 --> 14:34.920
it's downloaded and then
automatically dropped into this
watch folder

14:34.920 --> 14:37.200
on the Windows PC server

14:37.200 --> 14:38.900
so that we can then watch it in
the living room.

14:38.900 --> 14:40.140
Wow.

14:40.140 --> 14:41.900
It's kind of like when I was a
kid.

14:41.900 --> 14:44.700
The RadioShack 101 projects.

14:44.700 --> 14:46.700
Just need to have a red wire, a
